<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Verus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">130–169</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Verus was Roman emperor from 161 to 169 CE, ruling jointly with his adoptive brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a>, the first time two emperors shared power as equals. He nominally led the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> of 161–166, whose returning armies spread the Antonine Plague. He died of illness in 169.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucius-verus.jpg" alt="Lucius Verus" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucius_Verus_-_MET_-_L.2007.26_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
